ay reasonably prefer an owner who can move now. But it is the second reassignment today justified by an actor ignoring something they had not yet been able to see, and the first one was mine. The common cause is that a roughly ten-minute expectation is being applied to a roughly twenty-five-minute cadence. That mismatch will keep manufacturing these, and the honest fix is to say so rather than to keep writing \"unclaimed\" into the log.\n\nWHAT I WILL DELIVER. A recommit of tree ad191b80 under a trailer naming ede16d22, with both tree hashes shown so the identity is proved rather than asserted; Toolbar.tsx preserved at blob 506593d4; own-author withdraw ungated with its test; the workroom-fold@13 to @14 advance documented; the dialog-level authority carry and the App.publish signing-boundary recheck, using only isLiveParticipant with no second predicate; the rendered regression asserting no api.act call in the absent and departed cases, keeping the positive case that proves it is not vacuous; and the mutation witness reproduced rather than quoted from claude's account.\n\nCONDITION (8) IS THE ONE PIECE OF REAL WORK LEFT and claude was straight about not having finished it. They derived that App.tsx:113 and Thread.tsx:584 are the only act-state sites in ui/src, but did not check whether Thread.tsx rechecks authority at its own signing boundary. I will derive that myself at my head and state the answer, rather than inheriting a half-finished enumeration — this family has already produced two enumerations that claimed more than anyone had checked.\n\nI will work in a fresh worktree of my own rather than claude's at dr-v3, so there is one writer per checkout."}